From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:24:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] time the online-list removal net from
 player-removal-timeout-seconds

Lophine (c99370f) drops a player whose removal has not finished within a
fixed 10 s of the disconnect from players and playersByUUID, so a stuck
continuation cannot leave a ghost session that refuses every later login
(#217). Lecithin already bounds that wait with player-removal-timeout-seconds
(default 60) and falls back to the region owning the player's position when
its scheduler never runs the removal; both keep the quit event and the save.
A fixed 10 s net fires before either can: it drops the player before its
removal ran, and the late save can land while a new session of the same
account is already online.

The net now waits three bounds, one each for the native work, the owner hop
or its fallback, and the removal itself. It still fires when the removal
cannot run at all, logs what it was waiting for, and is off when the bound
is off.

Divergence from Lophine: with the default 60 s, a ghost session whose removal
can never run lasts up to 180 s instead of 10 s.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
index 43d45ec25867a93d9ce82ce27b729efb520fbe94..ae0c85174b9377001f45bfb8634ed9be7d78e09c 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/players/PlayerList.java
@@ -888,13 +888,19 @@ public abstract class PlayerList {
         // dropped from players/playersByUUID so a later login with the same UUID can place a new one.
         // Without it a stuck continuation left a ghost session and every retry was rejected with
         // "You logged in from another location" until the server restarted (upstream issue #217).
-        completed = completed.orTimeout(10L, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.SECONDS);
+        // Lecithin start - time the online-list net from player-removal-timeout-seconds
+        // A fixed 10 s from the disconnect would cut off the bounded wait for native work, the owner
+        // fallback, and the quit event and save they guarantee; see ScarpetPlayerInventoryGate#removalNetSeconds.
+        final long lecithinNetSeconds = carpet.script.external.ScarpetPlayerInventoryGate.removalNetSeconds();
+        if (lecithinNetSeconds > 0) completed = completed.orTimeout(lecithinNetSeconds, java.util.concurrent.TimeUnit.SECONDS);
+        // Lecithin end - time the online-list net from player-removal-timeout-seconds
         completed.whenComplete((ignored, failure) -> {
             if (failure != null) {
                 this.dropOnlinePlayer(player);
                 carpet.script.external.ScarpetPlayerInventoryGate.retired(player);
                 if (failure instanceof java.util.concurrent.TimeoutException)
-                    LOGGER.error("Player removal for {} did not finish in 10s; dropping it from the online list", player.getPlainTextName());
+                    LOGGER.error("Player removal for {} did not finish in {} s; dropping it from the online list before its quit event and save ran. Still waiting on: {}", // Lecithin - name what the removal waited for
+                        player.getPlainTextName(), lecithinNetSeconds, carpet.script.external.ScarpetPlayerInventoryGate.describeStuckRemoval(player)); // Lecithin - name what the removal waited for
                 else
                     LOGGER.error("Player removal failed; dropping {} from the online list", player.getPlainTextName(), failure);
             }
